{"id": "medi-cal-fraud-exceptions-outnumber-suspensions", "title": "Medi-Cal fraud: 339 exceptions to stop payment against 97 suspensions", "seconds": 105.8, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.024, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "e139b2a9a10fecd4", "words": 311, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]"], "text": "In five years, California stopped paying 97 Medi-Cal providers facing a credible allegation of fraud.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.84, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "97", "label": "payment suspensions", "sub": "credible allegations of fraud, five years"}, "emph": ["97"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.95, 1.56, 1.84, 2.12, 2.74, 3.19, 3.74, 4.1, 4.18, 4.61, 5.15, 5.25]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0]", "amount"], "text": "In 339 cases, it granted an exception, and kept paying.", "t0": 5.96, "t1": 10.0, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "339", "label": "exceptions: payments kept going", "sub": "all at the prosecutors’ request"}, "emph": ["339"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.44, 0.7, 1.24, 1.89, 2.06, 2.39, 2.49, 3.18, 3.45, 3.68]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "That’s 3.5 exceptions for every suspension.", "t0": 10.52, "t1": 13.21, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["3.5", "to", "1"], "sub": "exceptions for every suspension"}, "emph": ["3.5"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.53, 0.83, 1.12, 1.65, 1.85, 2.06]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[1]", "links[3]"], "text": "These are the State health department’s own figures, in its reply to the federal Medicaid agency.", "t0": 13.33, "t1": 17.88, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Reply of 17 February 2026", "text": "The State health department’s own figures, in its reply to the federal Medicaid agency.", "mark": "own figures"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.34, 0.44, 0.72, 0.95, 1.45, 1.63, 2.29, 2.47, 2.61, 2.98, 3.09, 3.22, 3.54, 4.01]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "headline", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "links[3]"], "text": "In January 2026, the federal Medicaid agency wrote to the Governor, asking for a program-integrity action plan.", "t0": 18.1, "t1": 24.93, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "headline", "date": "2026-01-27", "kicker": "The federal Medicaid agency writes to the Governor", "text": "A program-integrity action plan"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.72, 1.0, 1.95, 2.11, 2.45, 2.95, 3.44, 3.68, 3.77, 3.89, 4.57, 4.97, 5.13, 5.22, 6.18, 6.49]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "headline", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "links[3]"], "text": "The State’s reply came in February.", "t0": 25.05, "t1": 26.79, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "headline", "date": "2026-01-27", "kicker": "The federal Medicaid agency writes to the Governor", "text": "A program-integrity action plan"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 0.83, 1.04, 1.14]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Under federal rules, when a provider faces a credible allegation of fraud, payments stop.", "t0": 26.91, "t1": 31.64, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "question", "name": "Credible allegation of fraud", "sub": "against a provider"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Federal rules", "sub": "payments stop"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Unless good cause", "sub": "most often, prosecutors ask"}], "kicker": "The rule"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.64, 1.11, 1.31, 1.37, 1.83, 2.19, 2.27, 2.68, 3.2, 3.29, 3.98, 4.38]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "Unless there’s good cause.", "t0": 31.76, "t1": 32.99, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "question", "name": "Credible allegation of fraud", "sub": "against a provider"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "Federal rules", "sub": "payments stop"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Unless good cause", "sub": "most often, prosecutors ask"}], "kicker": "The rule"}, "emph": ["good cause"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.62, 0.84]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[0]", "story[2]"], "text": "The commonest good cause: prosecutors ask, because they don’t want the suspect warned.", "t0": 33.11, "t1": 37.79, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a suspended provider knows it is under investigation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.53, 0.76, 1.55, 2.23, 2.65, 2.96, 3.14, 3.39, 3.62, 3.74, 4.25]}, {"scene": "rule", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "A suspended provider knows it’s under investigation.", "t0": 37.91, "t1": 40.56, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "a suspended provider knows it is under investigation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.61, 1.14, 1.38, 1.53, 1.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[1]", "links[2]"], "text": "All 339 exceptions came at the prosecutors’ request.", "t0": 40.78, "t1": 44.24, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Payments continue", "kicker": "339 exceptions", "sub": "all at the prosecutors’ request"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.45, 0.73, 1.26, 1.84, 2.08, 2.18, 2.3, 2.92]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "So here the exception is the usual outcome, not the rare one.", "t0": 44.36, "t1": 47.47, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Payments continue", "kicker": "339 exceptions", "sub": "all at the prosecutors’ request"}, "emph": ["usual outcome"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.43, 0.56, 1.09, 1.21, 1.34, 1.67, 2.3, 2.52, 2.65, 2.9]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "links[0]"], "text": "Then how many cases reached a charge? The State sent 408 referrals to its fraud prosecutors.", "t0": 47.69, "t1": 53.11, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "408", "label": "credible-fraud referrals to the State fraud prosecutors", "sub": "five review years"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.43, 0.66, 1.11, 1.4, 1.48, 2.25, 2.42, 2.74, 3.0, 3.25, 3.48, 3.65, 4.13, 4.27, 4.4, 4.7]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Charges had been filed on 34.", "t0": 53.23, "t1": 55.06, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "34", "label": "charged, as of December 2025", "sub": "of 408 referrals"}, "emph": ["34"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.5, 0.7, 1.04, 1.16]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "13 ended in a judgment or restitution. 67 were declined.", "t0": 55.58, "t1": 59.81, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "408 referrals, as of December 2025", "rows": [["Charged", "34"], ["Judgment or restitution", "13"], ["Declined", "67"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.53, 0.8, 0.91, 1.01, 1.42, 1.57, 2.78, 3.53, 3.69]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "So many providers kept being paid under an allegation never tested in court.", "t0": 59.93, "t1": 63.82, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "an allegation that was never tested in court"}, "emph": ["never tested"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.42, 0.94, 1.16, 1.42, 1.73, 1.95, 2.07, 2.74, 3.03, 3.4, 3.53]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "Recoveries did rise: 11 million dollars in 2020-21.", "t0": 64.04, "t1": 67.96, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Recoveries, 2020-21", "$11.0 million"], "b": ["Recoveries, 2024-25", "$136.0 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.56, 0.79, 1.48, 1.85, 2.14, 2.48, 2.58, 2.9, 3.22, 3.31]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "By 2024-25, 136 million.", "t0": 68.08, "t1": 72.12, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Recoveries, 2020-21", "$11.0 million"], "b": ["Recoveries, 2024-25", "$136.0 million"]}, "emph": ["136 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.5, 1.12, 1.22, 2.33, 2.59, 2.9, 3.57]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "And the federal agency is recouping 1.8 billion dollars from eight jurisdictions.", "t0": 72.24, "t1": 76.5, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "California: more than $1.6 billion", "kicker": "Being recouped", "sub": "of $1.8 billion, from eight jurisdictions with State-only programs"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.24, 0.61, 1.05, 1.21, 1.75, 1.98, 2.25, 2.44, 2.81, 3.15, 3.32, 3.49]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "More than 1.6 billion of it from California.", "t0": 76.62, "t1": 79.31, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "California: more than $1.6 billion", "kicker": "Being recouped", "sub": "of $1.8 billion, from eight jurisdictions with State-only programs"}, "emph": ["1.6 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.39, 0.63, 0.93, 1.24, 1.64, 1.76, 1.85, 2.02]}, {"scene": "money", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]"], "text": "The State says prosecutors now ask for fewer exceptions.", "t0": 79.43, "t1": 82.27, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Fewer exceptions now", "sub": "the State’s account"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 0.65, 1.35, 1.56, 1.75, 1.91, 2.2]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The figures don’t show that any exception let a provider keep money it shouldn’t have.", "t0": 82.49, "t1": 86.41, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any exception let a provider keep money it should not have had", "Anything specific to San Francisco", "How many excepted providers were later charged"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.5, 0.72, 0.99, 1.14, 1.33, 1.89, 2.06, 2.14, 2.64, 2.91, 3.2, 3.3, 3.64]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Or how many excepted providers were later charged. And nothing is broken out for San Francisco.", "t0": 86.53, "t1": 91.48, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any exception let a provider keep money it should not have had", "Anything specific to San Francisco", "How many excepted providers were later charged"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.35, 0.58, 1.03, 1.54, 1.71, 1.98, 2.72, 2.94, 3.27, 3.38, 3.77, 3.95, 4.1, 4.3]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The outcome of each exception.", "t0": 91.6, "t1": 94.2, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The outcome of each exception"}, {"who": "", "what": "Whether any referred provider is paid by the City or its health plan"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.32, 0.63, 1.17, 1.35, 1.72, 1.83, 2.01]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "And whether the City or its health plan pays any referred provider.", "t0": 94.32, "t1": 98.05, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The outcome of each exception"}, {"who": "", "what": "Whether any referred provider is paid by the City or its health plan"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.52, 0.67, 1.13, 1.36, 1.52, 1.78, 2.11, 2.45, 2.78, 3.19]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "These are the State’s own figures. No provider is named, and none is accused here.", "t0": 98.17, "t1": 102.69, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.3, 0.4, 0.79, 0.97, 1.88, 2.09, 2.58, 2.71, 3.16, 3.38, 3.61, 3.74, 4.21]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 102.81, "t1": 104.87, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.62, 0.78, 1.0, 1.08, 1.18, 1.43, 1.71]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Stopped, or kept paying", "rule": "The rule", "lead1": "The exception, as the rule", "lead2": "Few reach a charge", "money": "The money", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "contrast"}